  "href": "/collections/zybach/elliott/maps/",
  "register": "Elliott State Forest map register (link records to Bob Zybach's ORWW originals)",
  "index_page_introduction_verbatim": "These maps are selected from the reports, magazine and news articles, government records and other documents contained in this website. They show the Elliott in reference to the State of Oregon; in relation to the other State Forests; legal boundaries; streams; topography; subbasins; fire history; early historical Oregon Indian Tribes; roads and trails; marbled murrelet, spotted owl, and coho habitat; tree ages; ownership history, and routes and locations of three Elliott Forest oral history tours conducted with Jerry Phillips during Fall 2017. Most of the maps are 200 d.p.i (dots per inch) JPEGS, sized to print on copy paper or display on a large desktop computer screen; a few are 200 d.p.i. PDF files that can be printed to full-size widths of 22- to 36-inches.",
  "method_notes": [
    "Link records only. Nothing was downloaded; each record points at the public file on orww.org and carries what HEAD reports.",
    "The MAPS page is a table of alternating thumbnail rows and caption rows. Captions are taken verbatim from the caption-row anchor text (HTML entities unescaped, <em> stripped); title_verbatim carries exactly that string.",
    "33 captioned map links are on the MAPS page (not ~35): several captions are JPEG/PDF pairs of one map (Ross A, Ross B, Elliott Forest ca. 1930, ODOT Coos-2, ODOT Douglas-1). map_group ties the pair together.",
    "One caption points outside the Maps folder (../References/Academic/OR_Fish_&_Wildlife/...); the URL is resolved against the page, not rewritten.",
    "The 10 oral-history route maps under History/Oral/Maps/ have NO caption anywhere in Bob's HTML — the folder is served as a bare Apache index. Their titles are derived from the filenames and are flagged in title_note; title_verbatim is null for all ten.",
    "related_interview_date is set only where the route-map filename date equals an oral-history folder date under History/Oral/ (2017-10-10, 2017-11-08, 2017-12-06, 2018-10-10).",
    "date comes from the filename (YYYYMMDD, YYYYMM, YYYY, or \"ca_YYYY\"); date_precision records which. A 00 day or 00 month is downgraded, not invented.",
    "Two files (Ross_20180222-A-26.pdf and Ross_20180222-B-26.pdf) are published by Bob at BOTH /Elliott_Forest/Maps/ and /Elliott_Forest/History/Oral/Maps/ with identical Content-Length; both records are kept and cross-noted rather than one being dropped."
  ],
